    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented project tracking as a full-stack, additive change \u2014 a second entity (`Project`) that belongs to a `Client`, with the list showing the client's **name** via a server-side join.\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V3__projects.sql`)\n- New `projects` table with `name` and a `client_id` FK to `clients`.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST + Spring beans, all new files)\n- `Project` entity, `NewProject` request body, and `ProjectView` DTO (id, name, clientName).\n- `ProjectRepository.findAllViews()` \u2014 JPQL constructor expression joining projects to clients to return each project with its client's name.\n- `ProjectsGet` / `ProjectsPost` logic classes wired by `projects.GET.yml` / `projects.POST.yml` under `rest/api/` (so paths are `/api/*`). POST validates name + existing client, returning 400 otherwise.\n- Extended `TestSupportController`: seeds `projects` from the fixture (using explicit ids via `JdbcTemplate`), and `reset` now truncates `projects` and `clients` with `RESTART IDENTITY`, toggling H2 referential integrity so the FK doesn't block the truncate.\n\n**Front-end** (new files only, following the five rules)\n- `routes/projects.index.tsx` \u2014 the page.\n- `features/projects/nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `nav-projects` link filling `AppNav`.\n- `features/projects/ProjectsTable.tsx` \u2014 list keyed on `['projects']`, rows expose `project-name` / `project-client`.\n- `features/projects/ProjectForm.tsx` \u2014 a `<select>` (`project-form-client`, option values = client ids) populated from the shared `['clients']` key; the write mutates and invalidates `['projects']`.\n- `features/projects/queries.ts` \u2014 the query/mutation helpers; no cross-feature imports (it shares the `['clients']` key rather than importing the clients feature).\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly. Typecheck passes and both `@core` Playwright tests pass.",
